WEBVTT

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.940
Ta da!

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.240
Ooh! That's a flyer for Card 
Capital's Shop Tournament!

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:11.860
Huh?

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.950
Hehe... They were handing 
them out at the store.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.670
Oh! The one that you guys mentioned before.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:23.450
Yup! Where all the confident regulars of the shop
test their skills against each other in battle!

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:25.850
Then, do you think that Kai...

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.140
I dunno about that guy.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:31.590
He's not actually a regular at the 
shop, so I don't think he'll show.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.390
Well, it doesn't matter who shows up,

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:37.290
it's obvious that I'll be the winner.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:42.920
Oh, what am I to do? My name's going 
to rise even higher in the ranks!

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.680
Application for participation 
in the Shop Tournament...

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.450
Deadline is... tomorrow?

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:50.710
Aichi, you're not entering, right?

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.910
You said so earlier, remember?

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.540
That's right! You said you'll 
cheer for my great victory!

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.730
I'm countin' on ya!

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.310
What are you looking at?

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:46.090
Emi...

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:49.850
Shop Tournament? They have those, too?

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.200
You gonna enter, Aichi?

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:55.610
Well, I heard all the people in the 
tournament will be really good...

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.430
Oh, I see...

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:00.060
I guess that would make it 
impossible for you, Aichi.

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.330
I mean, you're still a beginner. 
You're not any good yet, right?

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.080
You enter something like that, and 
you're just asking for a beat-down...

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.150
Yeah... You're right, I know.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.130
Emi, can you help me for a sec?

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:15.800
Coming!

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:24.790
What a stupid idea...

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:26.900
Me? In a tournament?

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.350
But...

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.900
This deck that I just reworked...

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:37.360
I wish I could try it out.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.110
The King of Knights, Alfred...

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:46.660
I got this card at that mysterious shop...

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:51.710
With this, my other cards can truly shine...

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:01.420
The King of Knights Enters the Fray!

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:14.100
It's the Card Capital Shop Tournament!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.900
An event that only happens twice a year!

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:19.620
Only two spots left!

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.810
Any fighter out there thinking 
"this is for me!" -- apply now!

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:24.910
Man, I'm so nervous...

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.120
I don't have the confidence...

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:33.100
Hey, did you hear? All the guys who've 
signed up are, like, crazy good!

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:36.610
There's no way I'd win if I entered...

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:40.350
U-Uh... Maybe I'll try out my 
new deck some other time...

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.180
Ooh, Aichi!

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.980
Aichi, you're entering, right?

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.150
No, I'm...

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:56.530
Yes. I think you would put up a good 
fight in the tournament, Aichi.

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.000
Just fill in this application.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:04:59.810
Come on.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.410
Manager, I just don't have the confidence!

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:05.900
Huh?

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:11.560
Kai...

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:13.010
Take it.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:15.930
Kai! You're entering?

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:19.660
There might be people I haven't met yet.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.890
People who are worth fighting.

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.970
Okay! Now there's only one spot left!

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.540
So, any other takers? First come first serve!

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:35.770
I'll enter!

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:43.280
Uh...

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.280
Name... Grade..

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:48.030
Leave the application here.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:50.490
All finished!

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:58.010
It looks like <i>I</i> was 0.1 seconds faster.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:01.490
Now... Please certify my application.

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:04.210
Osamu Kishida... First Year High School?

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:06.250
Oh, my...

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:08.910
Excuse me, but please let me enter instead!

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:11.090
I want to enter the tournament, 
no matter what it takes!

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:13.580
Well, as do I. So I can't 
just let you take my spot.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.710
But, if you truly insist,

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:19.710
you will need prove to me that you 
submitted the application first.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:20.680
Uh...

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:24.270
Now, tell me what year, what month, 
what day, what hour, what minute,

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.910
and what second you placed that application!

00:06:26.830 --> 00:06:28.210
Show me proof!

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:31.200
Can't we work this out like adults?

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:34.560
If you can't prove it, then I win.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.130
Now take that application 
with you and begone!

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.690
P-Please wait!

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:40.170
Okay, that's far enough.

00:06:40.660 --> 00:06:45.670
I am very happy to have two people so 
passionate about entering my tournament.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:48.740
But the tournament draw 
won't work out like this...

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:50.390
So, what will you do?

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:51.700
Manager?

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:52.700
Oh!

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.350
Shop Tournament?

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:57.770
Fight for the Last Entry Spot!

00:06:57.770 --> 00:07:00.900
He must have planned to do 
this from the beginning...

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.520
One shrewd manager, he is...

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:05.690
Hey, come on... This looks 
like it'll be interesting!

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.160
So, there you have it.

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.840
Whoever wins will get 
to enter the tournament.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.100
How about it?

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.430
Understood.

00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.990
Well, sounds fine by me. I'll get a bit of 
practice before the actual tournament.

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.340
Don't make me laugh.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:30.210
It's pointless for me 
to fight you as you are.

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:34.650
Kai did say that to me back then...

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:38.770
But if I can enter the Shop Tournament, 
I have a chance to fight Kai!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.250
For that chance, I must win...

00:07:41.630 --> 00:07:43.360
No matter what!

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:50.960
Kai, why're you watching Aichi's fight?

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:52.200
Not worth your time, wasn't he?

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:55.040
It's not him, it's Specs over there.

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:57.950
I've never played that guy before.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:00.750
Let's just see what he's made of.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.540
Are the two of you ready?

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.330
Yes!

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:11.260
Any time.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.930
Now then... Everyone, picture it!

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.690
Stand up! Vanguard!

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:25.180
Madame Mirage... I've never 
seen that unit before...

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:30.950
With that look on your face, it's like you've 
never fought against Megacolony units before...

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:34.310
I can see it now...

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:37.380
I can see you, suffering 
through this painful fight!

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:40.700
Here I go!

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.630
I ride Wingal!

00:08:48.490 --> 00:08:52.010
I use Barcgal's skill to 
move him to the rear row.

00:08:55.030 --> 00:08:57.910
Barcgal can do that?

00:08:57.910 --> 00:09:02.780
It's a skill you can use when 
another Royal Paladin unit appears.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.640
In this case, it was Wingal.

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:11.230
I'm impressed that Aichi has gotten 
this skilled with his units...

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:14.960
Barcgal, call your friends!

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:21.970
With Barcgal's skill, I move Flogal 
from my deck to a rear-guard circle.

00:09:31.830 --> 00:09:33.140
I am finished.

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:35.050
I don't understand you.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:39.210
What benefits will you get from
assembling so many weaklings?

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:40.680
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:44.730
I ride... Phantom Black!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.350
I call the Embodiment of Armor, Bahr!

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:58.570
Bahr? That's not a Megacolony unit!

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:02.280
It is a card from a different clan.

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:04.580
Assembling allies isn't always a good thing.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:10.590
When you mix units of different clans, you 
get two types of grade 1s with 8000 power!

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:11.950
I have more power!

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:17.600
Now then... I attack Wingal with Bahr!

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.700
I check for a damage trigger...

00:10:26.460 --> 00:10:30.610
I attack Wingal a second 
time with Phantom Black!

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:35.120
And, drive trigger... check.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.080
Check for a damage trigger...

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:44.990
Two damage.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.950
Exactly as I planned.

00:10:48.530 --> 00:10:50.750
I'm backed into a corner so soon...

00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:56.880
I can't fight Kai like this.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:04.540
Here I go.

00:11:09.210 --> 00:11:10.520
I'm not gonna lose!

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.320
I'm not gonna lose!

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.200
Stand up, my avatar!

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:31.150
Ride Blaster Blade!

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:44.810
I call the Knight of Silence, Gallatin, 
and the Little Sage, Marron!

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:51.900
I boost with Barcgal to power up Gallatin.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:56.780
Attack Phantom Black!

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.200
Check for a damage trigger...

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:07.760
I boost with Flogal to 
power up Blaster Blade...

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:12.410
And attack Phantom Black once again!

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.730
Check for a drive trigger...

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:23.210
Check for a damage trigger...

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:25.300
Next.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:27.590
I attack Phantom with Marron!

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.540
I guard with the Lizard Soldier, Ganlu!

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.690
Now both of them have two damage apiece!

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:45.980
My calculations seem to 
have been slightly off...

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:48.760
I'll show you true pain now.

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:55.370
I ride Bloody Hercules!

00:13:00.450 --> 00:13:03.340
And I call another Bloody Hercules!

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:05.380
I move Bahr to the back.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:09.560
And I call this Karma Queen!

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:16.580
Karma Queen, counterblast!

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:23.180
Using this card's skill, Gallatin
cannot stand up during your next turn!

00:13:23.180 --> 00:13:24.190
Say what?

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:31.700
Prostrate yourself before 
the might of the Queen!

00:13:36.990 --> 00:13:38.060
Oh, no...

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:41.840
Karma Queen has a power like that?

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:45.910
This is how we do things in Megacolony...

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:49.840
We bind our opponent's units, 
and prevent them from moving.

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:54.930
You will not be able to attack with
Gallatin during the next turn!

00:13:57.390 --> 00:14:02.350
I attack Blaster Blade with 
my rear-guard Bloody Hercules!

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:05.830
I guard with Marron!

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.560
Wait, there's more!

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:16.380
I attack Blaster Blade 
with my Vanguard Hercules!

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:18.790
Check for a drive trigger!

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:23.180
Check for a damage trigger...

00:14:24.440 --> 00:14:28.250
I power up Karma Queen by boosting with Bahr!

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:31.000
And I attack Blaster Blade!

00:14:35.390 --> 00:14:37.170
I check for a damage trigger...

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:42.770
Now, it is your turn.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:47.280
With Gallatin's movements sealed, you 
won't be able to mount a serious attack.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:51.780
By my calculations, my victory 
is all but guaranteed.

00:14:56.020 --> 00:14:56.900
Kai?

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.290
Specs there isn't anything special.

00:15:00.180 --> 00:15:01.940
He hasn't noticed yet.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:07.280
He hasn't noticed why Aichi gathered 
all those Royal Paladins...

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:10.890
Draw.

00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.080
It's finally time...

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:24.170
Please... Give me and my friends the power!

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:26.770
Enter the fray!

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.190
I ride the ruler of all knights...

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:42.510
The King of Knights, Alfred!

00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.190
Alfred?!

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:48.600
Whoa! That's the top card 
of the Royal Paladins!

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:52.560
I move Marron, and call Gancelot.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.660
With Alfred there... that lineup...

00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:00.980
Oh, shoot!

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:04.430
I attack your vanguard Hercules with Alfred!

00:16:07.430 --> 00:16:09.650
First check of the twin drive...

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:12.440
Second check...

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.450
Llew? This is bad!

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:18.680
I got a critical trigger!

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.370
Effect number one:

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:23.610
Alfred's damage is +1.

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:26.800
Second, I add +5000 to Gancelot's power!

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.470
Also, Alfred's own skill...

00:16:29.790 --> 00:16:34.980
He gains +2000 power for each 
Royal Paladin rear-guard in play!

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:37.930
2000 times five... 10000 power?

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.280
This is Alfred's power!

00:16:43.660 --> 00:16:47.610
My Royal Paladin units are used 
to their fullest potential!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.740
Check for a damage trigger!

00:16:57.050 --> 00:16:58.250
And the second...

00:16:59.230 --> 00:17:01.530
I got a damage trigger, yes!

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:06.730
By the Demonic Dragon Mage, Rakshasa's 
skill, I add +5000 power to my vanguard Hercules!

00:17:08.180 --> 00:17:10.230
Power 15000?

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:16.430
In that case, I boost the powered-up 
Gancelot with Marron and attack Hercules!

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:20.010
I guard with Rakshasa!

00:17:23.660 --> 00:17:25.960
Now your attack won't get through!

00:17:33.500 --> 00:17:35.570
It isn't over yet.

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:39.660
Give me the power... From the depths of
 hell itself, the embodiment of evil...

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:42.330
I ride Hell Spider!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.570
Hell Spider, counterblast!

00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:50.670
Next turn, Gallatin cannot stand up!

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.720
Hell Spider has that power, too?

00:17:57.410 --> 00:18:00.430
Too bad this effect can only 
be used on rear-guards...

00:18:01.260 --> 00:18:04.880
I would sure like to seal
 Alfred in this situation.

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:08.570
I call two Phantom Blacks!

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:13.010
I power up Hercules by boosting 
with Phantom Black!

00:18:13.600 --> 00:18:15.740
Attack Alfred!

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:18.040
I guard with the Future Knight, Llew!

00:18:30.010 --> 00:18:33.630
I boost with Phantom, and 
power up Hell Spider!

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:37.930
Attack Alfred for a second time!

00:18:40.160 --> 00:18:42.210
I guard with Isolde.

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:46.820
I activate Isolde's skill...

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:48.820
I drop Wingal from my hand,

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:52.270
and, using that skill, nullify 
the attack on Alfred!

00:18:55.930 --> 00:18:58.280
Check the twin drive... First check!

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:00.640
Second check!

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:02.300
I'm not done yet!

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:06.430
I boost Karma Queen with 
Bahr, and attack Alfred!

00:19:06.430 --> 00:19:08.750
I guard with Elaine!

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:15.580
It won't break through to Alfred!

00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:18.270
Three attacks, all for nothing!

00:19:18.270 --> 00:19:21.480
This was not in any of my calculations!

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:30.080
I retire Gallatin, and 
call Wingal in its place.

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:35.180
He replaced Gallatin with Wingal?

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:37.730
His new Wingal isn't sealed!

00:19:38.030 --> 00:19:39.750
He can attack with it!

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:43.990
Now he can attack three times!

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:46.750
Gancelot, boosted by Marron...

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:48.460
Attack Hell Spider!

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.530
I guard with Aermo!

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:57.200
Furthermore, I intercept 
with Hercules's Skill!

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:10.100
I've got cards that can 
intercept too, you know.

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:13.700
Wingal... Do it for the immobilized Gallatin!

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:16.740
I boost with Barcgal...

00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.530
...and attack Hell Spider!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.630
Check for a damage trigger...

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:29.580
That makes 5 damage.

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:31.220
And now, I'll finish it with this!

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:35.130
I attack Hell Spider with Alfred!

00:20:36.190 --> 00:20:38.480
All his loyal Royal Paladins

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:41.680
give Alfred +2000 power!

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:58.770
It's over.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:04.690
It has been decided that Aichi Sendou 
gets to enter the Shop Tournament!

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:07.640
You go, dude!

00:21:12.100 --> 00:21:14.500
That was quite an entertaining fight.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:20.590
I think you may be able to put up a 
good fight at the Shop Tournament.

00:21:20.910 --> 00:21:26.110
According to my calculations, the chance 
of that happening is approximately 85%.

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:30.140
Uh, thanks... But how exactly 
did you calculate that?

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:31.700
Putting that aside...

00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:33.310
Do your best.

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:34.590
Uh, thanks.

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:35.940
Congratulations, Aichi.

00:21:36.430 --> 00:21:39.390
I'm expecting good things from 
you at the Shop Tournament.

00:21:39.390 --> 00:21:40.400
Right!

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:43.580
Kai!

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:47.910
Looks like I might fight you 
at the Shop Tournament, Kai...

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:49.850
Your method of using Alfred...

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:51.800
That level is typical.

00:21:52.610 --> 00:21:57.100
To me, you are still not 
someone worth fighting.

00:21:58.730 --> 00:22:01.820
Don't mind him. He's one 
of <i>those</i> kind of guys.

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:08.180
What I wanted to say to Kai was that 
I'd win my way up the Shop Tournament,

00:22:08.630 --> 00:22:10.950
and make sure to fight him!

00:22:11.690 --> 00:22:14.770
If I combine the powers of my cards...

00:23:53.590 --> 00:23:55.060
What are you doing?

00:23:55.060 --> 00:23:57.500
You need courage to take 
that first step, right?

00:23:57.500 --> 00:24:00.500
I'm so nervous, I don't know
 what I'm doing anymore...

00:24:01.310 --> 00:24:04.290
You're so calm, Misaki... I 
bet this never happens to you.

00:24:04.290 --> 00:24:06.360
That's not true. It's the same for me.

00:24:06.360 --> 00:24:09.020
Next time: The Shop Tournament Begins!

00:24:09.020 --> 00:24:11.730
I'm actually entering the Shop Tournament!

00:24:11.730 --> 00:24:13.380
Picture it... Picture it...

00:24:13.380 --> 00:24:15.970
But everything I picture is negative!

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:17.520
Like I said, it's not just you.

00:24:17.520 --> 00:24:18.720
Everyone's the same way.
